	abstract = {Resonance-assisted photonic crystal ({PhC)} slab photodetectors are demonstrated by utilizing six 7-nm-thick {InGaAsP} quantum wells. In order to encourage efficient photon coupling into the slab from the vertical direction, a coupled-dipole-cavity-array {PhC} structure is employed. Inheriting the characteristics of the dipole mode, this resonant detector is highly polarization selective and shows a 22-nm-wide spectral width. The maximum responsivity of 0.28{\^a}{\^A}{\^A}{A/W}, which is {\textgreater}20 times larger than that of the identical detector without the pattern, is observed near 1.56{\^a}{\^A}{\^A}{\^I}{\OE}m.},
