	abstract = {Long{\^a}{\^A}{\^A}wavelength {InAs1{\^a}{\^A}{\^A}xSbx} photoconductors operated without cryogenic cooling are reported. The devices are based on {p{\^a}{\^A}{\^A}InAs1{\^a}{\^A}{\^A}xSbx/p{\^a}{\^A}{\^A}InSb} heterostructures grown on (100) semi{\^a}{\^A}{\^A}insulating {GaAs} substrates by low pressure metalorganic chemical vapor deposition ({LP{\^a}{\^A}{\^A}MOCVD).} Photoreponse up to 14 {\^I}{\OE}m has been obtained in a sample with x=0.77 at 300 K, which is in good agreement with the measured infrared absorption spectra. The corresponding effective lifetime of {\^a}{\^A}{\^A}0.14 ns at 300 K has been derived from stationary photoconductivity. The Johnson noise limited detectivity at {\^I}{\^A}»=10.6 {\^I}{\OE}m is estimated to be about 3.27{\~A}{\^A}107 cm{\^a}{\^A}{\^A}{Hz1/2/W} at 300 K. {\copyright} 1996 American Institute of Physics.},
