	abstract = {Using symmetry considerations, we identify three families of large photonic band-gap ({PBG)} architectures defined by the isointensity surfaces of four beam laser interference. For particular choices of beam intensities, directions, and polarizations, we obtain a diamondlike crystal, a novel body-centered cubic architecture, and a simple cubic structure with {PBG} to center frequency ratios of 25\$0, 21\$0, and 11\$0, respectively, when the isointensity surface defines a silicon (dielectric constant of 11.9) to air boundary.},
