	abstract = {The transmission of p- and s-polarized light through thin silver films as a function of wavelength and angle of incidence has been measured. As predicted, a dip in transmission occurs in the vicinity of the plasma frequency only for the p-polarized light. This dip is associated with the excitation of a collective-type surface plasma mode in the thin film by the electromagnetic wave. The plasma frequency of the film can be accurately determined from this dip to occur at 3.80 {eV.}},
