	abstract = {We use soft lithography replica molding to fabricate unclad polystyrene {(PS)} and clad {SU-8} microring resonator filters. The {PS} resonator has an intrinsic quality factor of 1.0{\~A}---104 at {\^I}{\^A}{\^A}¬{\^A}{\^A}ª=1.55 {\^I}{\^A}{\^A}¬{\^A}{\^A}ºm, while that of the {SU-8} resonator is 7100. The extinction ratios of the {PS} and {SU-8} microring filters are -12 and -20 {dB}, respectively, with net insertion losses of 6.7 and 9.9 {dB.} The good quality factors and high extinction ratios of the microring resonator filters show the practicality of soft-lithography replica molding for the fabrication of integrated optical devices.},
