	abstract = {Corrugated silicon nanocone (SiNC) arrays have been fabricated on a silicon wafer by two polystyrene-sphere-monolayer-masked etching steps in order to create high-performance antireflective coatings. The reflectance was reduced from above 35\% to less than 0.7\% in the range 400--1050 nm, and it remained below 0.5\% at incidence angles up to 70$\,^{\circ}$ at 632.8 nm for both s- and p-polarized light. The fluorinated corrugated SiNC array surface exhibits superhydrophobic properties with a water contact angle of 164$\,^{\circ}$. Open image in new window},
