@article{Schmidt:06,
	abstract = {In this paper, a generic process flow to fabricate silicon nanowire vertical surround-gate field-effect transistors (VS-FET) is presented. The intrinsic advantage of the process developed is that no chemical or mechanical polishing steps are needed, which are difficult to control at this length scale. In the demonstrated device, n-doped silicon nanowires grown epitaxially by CVD on a p-doped substrate were used as active material. In this process SiO<sub>2</sub> layers and Al gate metal are deposited by spin coating and reactive ion etching is used to free the Au/Si caps of the SiO<sub>2</sub> deposited nanowire. Output characteristics of an array of VS-FETs for different gate voltages are measured. The array of VS-FETs exhibited a gate-voltage-dependent current increase of more than two orders of magnitude. (10 refs.)},
