	abstract = {Control of crystalline orientation of germanium (Ge) on a SiO{sub 2} surface was demonstrated by lateral graphoepitaxy. An x-ray diffraction curve with a (400) peak was obtained in a Ge crystal grown on microholes, each of which has a side of 1 mu m long and four 10-nm-thick SiO{sub 2} sidewalls made from thermally oxidized Si {111} planes. Using this Ge crystal on the microholes as a seed crystal, a Ge crystal with a (400) orientation was laterally grown on a 10-nm-thick SiO{sub 2} layer, which was a thermally oxidized flat Si (100) surface, by zone melting. (9 refs.)},
