	abstract = {Silicon nanowires (SiNWs) were synthesized using laser ablation. A continuous SiNW film was prepared by grinding the pieces of sponge-like SiNWs to powder, then dispersing and sticking the powder onto a Si wafer. The field emission characteristics of the SiNW film were studied based on current-voltage measurements and the Fowler-Nordheim equation. The electron field emission increased with decreasing diameter of SiNWs. A hydrogen plasma treatment of the SiNW film aimed at reducing the oxide overlayer improved the emission uniformity of the film. (15 refs.)},
	author = {F. C. K. Au and K. W. Wong and Y. H. Tang and Y. F. Zhang and I. Bello and S. T. Lee},
