	abstract = {Monte Carlo simulations of electron impact ionization in silicon are presented which include the pseudopotential band structure as well as collision broadening and higher order effects in the electron-phonon interaction. Conduction in the two lowest conduction bands of silicon is considered. The authors also present new results for the impact ionization probability and deformation potential constants which are obtained by comparing their theory with a variety of experimental results. (13 refs.)},
