	abstract = {The Zener current in a constant field is calculated both with and without the {Wannier-Adams} reduction of the interband-coupling terms. The Zener current is only slightly different in the two cases, a fact which has already been noted by Wannier. The apparent reduction of interband coupling is interpreted as a polarization correction. A detailed calculation of the Zener current is made for a simple two-band model which is applicable to {InSb.} The evaluation of the tunneling integral follows closely a calculation due to Keldysh.},
